# Codex Review

Target: branch diff against origin/main

The oracle hook loses previously working protection for conditional sed writes. Read-only hook probes confirmed the regression; docs_check.py and diff whitespace checks passed. The full build/test gate was not run.

Review comment:

- [P2] Preserve sed protection inside shell conditionals — /home/joe/repos/ASTRA/.claude/hooks/guard-oracle.sh:212-214
  With the oracle guard unarmed, `if true; then sed -i 's/x/y/' tests/golden/example.hpp; fi` now returns 0, whereas the base hook returns 2. Removing the coarse sed matcher exposes a gap in the replacement parser: it identifies `then` as the command and never classifies the following `sed`. Ordinary conditional edits can therefore modify protected goldens or ADRs without the authorization required by [AGENTS.md:27–29](AGENTS.md#L27-L29). Recognize shell control-word prefixes before command classification and add a regression case before dropping the previous coverage.
